  "title": "HD-EEGtask(Dataset 2)",
  "description": "High-density EEG (256 electrodes) recorded in 20 right-handed healthy volunteers in Rennes, France, across four conditions: eyes-open resting state, visual naming, auditory naming, and a working memory (picture recognition) task. The dataset supports studies of functional brain connectivity and network dynamics during cognitive tasks.",
  "methods_description": "Data were recorded with an EGI HD-EEG system (256 electrodes) at a 1000 Hz sampling rate, with impedances kept below 5 kOhm. Each participant completed a 10-minute eyes-open resting state, naming of 80 pictures (with 40 scrambled pictures as no-response trials), naming of 80 sounds, and a memory task in which 80 pictures were shown, 40 of them previously seen, and participants pressed a button to indicate whether they had seen each one.",
